<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55948" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηφ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be downcast, to be mute</i> with horror or grief, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῆ δὲ κατηφήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.293
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκάχοντο κατήφησάν τ᾽ ἐνὶ θυμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.342
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.443
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δαὶ κατηφεῖς
			ὄμμα</span>; <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1012
			</span></i>; of animals, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				604b12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ κατηφήσαι [ἂν]
			θεός</span> and well <i>might</i> God <i>grieve</i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				3.8.4
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὓς κατέφησεν</span>
			).</div>
